{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QGeometricLanglands.TannakaKreinIsomorphism","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QGeometricLanglands.TannakaKreinIsomorphism","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Equivalence","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.isTannakaKreinDual_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.isTannakaKreinDual_refl","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/tannaka-krein-isomorphism.lean#L123-L140","doc":"Any category is Tannaka–Krein dual to itself over its own fibre functor.\n\n**Deliberately a `theorem` and not an `instance`.** As an instance it would\nbe *general* — quantified over every `C` and `τ` — so typeclass resolution\nwould discharge any `[IsTannakaKreinDual A B τR τC]` whose two sides happen\nto unify, silently, in a downstream result whose author meant them to be\ndifferent categories. The whole point of this class is that the hypothesis is\nhard; an instance that supplies it for free where the arguments coincide is a\ntrapdoor.\n\nContrast `instance : IsWeilZeta weilZetaExample` in\n`QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.WeilZeta`, which is an instance on a **concrete**\nwitness and therefore cannot fire spuriously. Generality is the difference,\nnot the fact of being a witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.tannaka_krein_isomorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.tannaka_krein_isomorphism","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/tannaka-krein-isomorphism.lean#L97-L109","doc":"The duality itself, as the conjecture's statement: given the hypothesis, an\nequivalence of categories over the fibre functors exists.\n\nA projection, and labelled as one. It exists so the conjecture has a name to\nbe cited by, not to suggest anything was derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsTannakaKreinDual.equiv_over_fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsTannakaKreinDual.equiv_over_fibre","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/tannaka-krein-isomorphism.lean#L95-L95","doc":"An equivalence of **categories** commuting with the fibre functors:\n`τ_C ∘ e ≅ τ_R`. One field rather than two, so that the compatibility is\nasserted of the same equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsTannakaKreinDual.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsTannakaKreinDual.mk","kind":"ctor","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/tannaka-krein-isomorphism.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsTannakaKreinDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsTannakaKreinDual","kind":"class","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/tannaka-krein-isomorphism.lean#L76-L95","doc":"**Tannaka–Krein duality, as a named hypothesis.**\n\n`RepLoc` and `ComodH` are the two categories; `τR` and `τC` are their fibre\nfunctors to a common target `E` (the fibre at the unit defect, in the\nnarrative). The single field says: there is an equivalence of categories\nbetween them *lying over the fibre functors*.\n\nParameters, not axioms — an instance must supply real categories and real\nfunctors, and then exhibit the equivalence. Nothing here is opaque. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:tannaka-krein-isomorphism","label":"conj:tannaka-krein-isomorphism","md":"quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/tannaka-krein-isomorphism.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}